      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we need to calculate the total duration over which the batteries are replaced and then identify the month based on that duration.\n\n1. **Identify the interval for changing batteries:**\n   - Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of 5-month intervals in 25 replacements:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total intervals} = 25 \\text{ replacements} \\times 5 \\text{ months per replacement} = 125 \\text{ months}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the month after 125 months:**\n   - Since January 1st is the starting point (May change the batteries the first time), we need to find the month 125 months later from May.\n\n4. **Calculate the number of years and extra months:**\n   - There are 12 months in a year. To find out how many complete years are in 125 months:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Months per year} = 12\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Whole years} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{125}{12} \\right\\rfloor = 10 \\text{ years}\n     \\]\n   - Calculate the remaining months after accounting for the complete years:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Remaining months} = 125 - (10 \\times 12) = 125 - 120 = 5 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Determine the month for the remaining 5 months:**\n   - Starting from May, we count forward 5 months:\n     \\[\n     \\text{May} + 1 \\text{ month} = June\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{June} + 1 \\text{ month} = July\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{July} + 1 \\text{ month} = August\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{August} + 1 \\text{ month} = September\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{September} + 1 \\text{ month} = October\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the batteries will be changed for the 25th time in the month of \\boxed{October}.",
